{"reference":"Revelation 16","book":"Revelation","chapter":16,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Har-magedon","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The gathering place in verse 16 is called in Hebrew Har-magedon. The chapter identifies it as the place where the kings are assembled before the seventh bowl, but the name’s derivation and geographical location remain uncertain. The passage therefore gives its narrative function clearly while leaving its precise identification open to dispute.","verse_refs":["Revelation 16:12-16"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_revelation_016_9a8f455061344d5a969b1c80"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]},{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"The Bowl Sequence in Revelation","blocks":[{"id":"block_2","text":"Revelation 16 belongs to the book’s larger pattern of sevenfold judgment sequences: seals, trumpets, and bowls, with recurring motifs and intervening scenes. Many interpreters also understand Revelation as repeatedly reworking Israel’s Scriptures, including Daniel, Ezekiel, Isaiah, Exodus, Zechariah, Genesis, and Psalms. These wider patterns help situate the bowls within the book’s symbolic and highly structured presentation.","verse_refs":["Revelation 10:1-11","Revelation 11:1-19","Revelation 12:1-17","Revelation 13:1-18","Revelation 14:1-20","Revelation 15:1-8","Revelation 17:1-18","Revelation 18:1-24","Revelation 19:1-21","Revelation 1:1-20","Revelation 20:1-15","Revelation 21:1-27","Revelation 22:1-21","Revelation 2:1-29","Revelation 3:1-22","Revelation 4:1-11","Revelation 5:1-14","Revelation 6:1-17","Revelation 7:1-17","Revelation 8:1-13","Revelation 9:1-21"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_revelation_016_15a957d6c115bbc0bf8922b4"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}